  "preamble": "Diphthongization of the close-mid back vowel [o] (usually long [oː]) to [ou]. Icelandic shows it regularly: Old Norse long ó became /ou/ (Old Norse bók > Icelandic bók [ˈpouːk] 'book'), while Swedish and Norwegian raised the same vowel to /uː/.",
